.TH HLM 1 "" "hlm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hlm \- the Helm command line client for people and agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hlm
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
hlm reads and changes a Helm task list. Every command is one or more calls of the MCP tools the agent uses on the same /mcp endpoint; hlm call reaches any tool directly. Without a command, hlm shows Today.
.PP
Task references: #42 or 42 (the task number), now (the now task) or the task id.
