.SH JSON OUTPUT
\-\-json (or HLM_FORMAT=json) prints the MCP tool's structuredContent exactly as an MCP client receives it. Fields may be added in a minor version; they are never removed or retyped within a major version. Errors go to standard error as one line: {"error":{"code","message","exitCode","retryable","clientId",...}}; standard output then stays empty. \-\-plain prints tab\-separated rows without headers.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a change that was already applied (no\-op)
.TP
.B 1
Other error (internal)
.TP
.B 2
Usage: unknown command or flag, bad value or date, \-\-yes missing, broken config.toml
.TP
.B 3
Authentication: no key (hlm login or HLM_API_KEY), or a wrong or revoked one
.TP
.B 4
Not found: no such task (#n), device or now task
.TP
.B 5
Server unavailable (network, timeout, HTTP 5xx): the change may have been applied; retry with the same \-\-client\-id. Also too many calls with the key (rate_limited): nothing was applied; run it again after the wait the message names
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (Ctrl\-C)
